A||||4||mshill||Removing roof skin?||||5||
Z||000000||mshill||07-14-2000||02:30 AM||||Do you have to remove the windshield to remove the top roof skin?  I need to replace mine and really did not want to have to pay for labor to replace the windshield.<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||07-14-2000||02:39 AM||||The windshield Does Not need to be removed. But you have to remove the black rubber trim that is around the windsheild and before you put it back on check to make sure the windshield seal isn't cracked or split. It is best to check it once the old roof is off.<BR>Then just install new roof and press in the rubber trim. If the trim is loose in areas you can put a dab of windshield sealant on the spot or just a thin coat on the entire trim. Gennerally it is near the top corners is where you need to put a dab of sealant. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||88 Fiero||07-14-2000||11:07 AM||||mshill....When I did the conversion on my long gone '88 hard top with the factory sunroof was a challenge... I fellow fiero member showed me how it ease and confidence of not breaking it... He said to used a fishing line one end on the outside of the old roof and the other end goes underneath of the roof and exit to the other side of the pillars....then pull it left to right like your sawing it..as you do that you start on the top and go all the way down...it's piece of cake and your cutting that black goo in there...good luck ...you'll be done before you know it..it doesnt take that long tho...let me know what happened...||||reg||1
Z||000003||lennyb4||07-14-2000||11:22 AM||||They also sell a tool (just wire and some rings attatched) at most auto-part stores.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||07-17-2000||02:34 AM||||Guys, thanks for the info.  I am actually removing the factory sunroof and putting a solid top on for my F50 kit.  The F50 just wouldn't look right with the cheesy Fiero sunroof on it.  I would turn around and sell the sunroof parts except the top skin is busted up at the top of the drivers side pillar.||||reg||1
